WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:04.379
♪♪

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.550
At the beginning of season two
we meet Alex

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.594
In a very serene place.

00:00:10.594 --> 00:00:12.596
All of the pain and the

00:00:12.596 --> 00:00:15.641
frustration that she had been
carrying around for

00:00:15.641 --> 00:00:16.975
years and years and years.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.603
I think she had to get out of
the chaos

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.899
Bradley’s doing anything to say
that she is compliant, 

00:00:23.899 --> 00:00:26.068
she’s ready to be a team player,

00:00:26.068 --> 00:00:28.528
but she also wants
autonomy.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.113
She thinks she’s in control

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:32.699
and we find out by the end of
episode one

00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:34.034
That is such an illusion.

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:37.579
You could have been my friend
but that did not happen.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:40.999
I am an so glad it did not
because all you had to do

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.085
was be honest with me.

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:44.753
At the end of season one

00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:46.797
There was an enormous thrill
that

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.757
Cory and Bradley shared,

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:51.468
in that Cory’s attachment to her
grew

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:53.804
in a way that was
unexpected to him.

00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:55.681
We don’t know If it’s just an
infatuation or

00:00:55.681 --> 00:00:58.600
it’s real but they are always
doing this dance

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.351
aound each other.

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:00.769
Camera's same mark.

00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:03.522
Coming into the second season
was really a different

00:01:03.522 --> 00:01:07.025
trip because we came in and shot
during covid

00:01:07.401 --> 00:01:11.863
We were all very excited to be
going back into production but

00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:13.282
also very scared.

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:16.410
We already started a season two

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:19.329
that then suddenly felt less
relevant.

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:27.129
When I read the new episode one
for season two

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.627
where you start
to feel all those little things

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:27.629
that we were not aware of then

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:28.964
the little sharing of food

00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:30.465
the the little sneezes.

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:31.842
Just thought that was very
smart.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:35.679
We shot a big big new years eve
sequence, In LA.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.140
We did Times Square as you would
outside

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:40.934
a gigantic parking lot, it's

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.979
basically large enough for huge
green screen signs.

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:46.064
It was really fun to shoot it

00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:48.984
and then create the world of
with VFX.

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:50.819
Standby camera two

00:01:51.737 --> 00:01:55.866
The dance number was great and
they only rehearsed it once

00:01:55.991 --> 00:01:57.743
An hour before we shot

00:01:57.826 --> 00:02:00.120
Because we wanted it to look not
rehearsed

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.415
To do that on one of my first
days on set

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:06.168
Especially while we were filming
during a pandemic

00:02:06.418 --> 00:02:08.045
To just have unbridled joy.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.173
It was so funny, I couldn’t stop
laughing on the day.

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:14.885
Everybody was like
2020 is my year.

00:02:15.218 --> 00:02:18.722
It was surreal to go back and
shoot the arrogance we all had

00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:20.932
on that day in December of 2019.

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:22.476
To Kerry’s credit

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:26.104
she really came up with an
incredible storyline

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:31.902
about what happens when the
world closes in while 

00:02:31.902 --> 00:02:34.654
you’re just making plans
for your own life.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.656
♪♪

